      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T15:59:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m far from an expert here, but it seems a little strange that `name` is the way to tell if the `drm_sched` still exists or not. This feels more like relying on hidden behavior rather than something explicit, since `name` isn\u0027t set to null in `drm_sched_fini()`.\n\nRather, I think checking `sched-\u003eready` is more appropriate:\n\n[src/third_party/kernel/v6.12/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c](https://source.corp.google.com/h/chrome-internal/chromeos/superproject/+/main:src/third_party/kernel/v6.12/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c;drc\u003d2da108b4b5fb7ec04d7e951418ed80e97f7c35ad;l\u003d1375)\n\n```\n/**\n * drm_sched_fini - Destroy a gpu scheduler\n *\n * @sched: scheduler instance\n *\n * Tears down and cleans up the scheduler.\n */\nvoid drm_sched_fini(struct drm_gpu_scheduler *sched)\n{\n...\n\tif (sched-\u003eown_submit_wq)\n\t\tdestroy_workqueue(sched-\u003esubmit_wq);\n\tsched-\u003eready \u003d false;         \u003c\u003c---- set to false here\n\tkfree(sched-\u003esched_rq);\n\tsched-\u003esched_rq \u003d NULL;       \u003c\u003c---- or could check this instead\n}\n```",
      "revId": "e5ec15a54325d5a0023d174fa468b6c1e53e692c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac3473a9_c2820aee",
