      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T17:53:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Me neither :) which is why I\u0027m trying to narrow the scope as much as possible here to just preventing it from crashing when accessing `name` if it doesn\u0027t exist, rather than trying to deal with `drm_sched`/fence lifecycles, will leave that for upstream.\n\nFor instance,`name` is alloc\u0027d by xe which apparently doesn\u0027t share a lifecycle with `drm_sched` so using `sched-\u003eready` won\u0027t work: http://cs/h/chrome-internal/chromeos/superproject/+/main:src/third_party/kernel/v6.12/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c?l\u003d1132\n\nI did add an extra check for `fence-\u003esched` just in case.",
